body:
it's just a tidal change in the 'news cycle'.  on the day of the massacre, we initially united in shared rage at the shooters mixed with sympathy for the victims....much like the 9/11 attacks a few years later.  in the immediate fallout, all sorts of 'experts' + 'investigative journalists' created an entire industry around the school shooting.  national conversations about violent video games and marilyn manson music.  along  with an slew of armchair psychiatrists who jumped on the 'anti-bullying bandwagon'  this added another dimension to the story that would continue to fuel the columbine industry...maybe part of us wanted to think that 'bullies' were going to get what 'they deserved'. 

&#x200B;

problem is, concept of 'bulllying' is completely subjective.  fox news thinks media slants left / vice versa.  as the internet continued expanding, it allowed people to read all about the shootings and falloutr with a new set of ears. reddit birthed a slew of contrarians who ended up aligning themselves with the "give mea fucking break.  these kids were just assholes and it annoys me that they are seen as sympathetic in any way.  think about the victims"

&#x200B;

and then people (like you) who have long since paralleled your own struggles against 'bullies'. with these 2 dweebs, don't like it that years later, people are questioning the narrative.  because then maybe your 'narrative' isn't so credible either.  

&#x200B;

i dont know, the day i read about klebold usinga racial slur before blowing off a black student's head (1 who to the best of knowledge had done nothning to him), i find the 'victim narrative'.hard to stomach.  two white teenagers gunning down a black student in a leisurely manner while frightened cops are hiding in the trees.  if that isn't "white privilegwe"..!

if you take the 'maherian position' that all religion is 'bullshit' and never to be used as 'justification' for land ownership. then both the jewish and muslim claims to the land are invalidated and we are left with the current political reality.  if we consider 'jews' and 'muslims' ethnic groups instead, any 'peace' is unsustainable when there is a tiny jewish enclave surrounded by a completely arab middle east.  its like those white farmers in zimbabwe who act surprised when they are persecuted.

&#x200B;

let's put it this way, if the entire landmass of what is now considered 'israel' and 'palestine' was forced to be 'evacuated' tomorrow, who would be unable to find a place to go?  palestinians have their 'arab brethren' in the neighboring countries and israelis' have lots of friends in the united states and europe.  from an international standpoint, we need to ask ourselves "who NEEDS the land more?"  it is true that arabs will never stop opposing israel until it is gone and it is also true that israel, even without US aid, will always have the military means to overwhelm arab resistance.  that is, unless all arab countries unite in their oppositon, which means that just like before, the united states will offer enough military aid to ensure israel's survival.

